# Amendment — structural-enforcement A3 TDD-guard
#
# 2026-04-28. Per the locked plan-doc
# `docs/rebuild/plans/structural-enforcement-a3-tdd-guard.md`
# and the locked research artefact
# `docs/rebuild/plans/research/structural-enforcement-a3-tdd-guard-research.md`.
#
# A3 is the SECOND gate-that-refuses in the structural-enforcement
# programme, after A2 (sealed at amendment #70). A2 refused Edits
# whose path didn't trace to a manifest-registered binding the
# active-scope sentinel admits. A3 refuses Edits that introduce
# code satisfying a NEW acceptance criterion without a test pinned
# to that AC landing in the same diff.
#
# Surface added (hands-off-lifecycle, sealed):
#
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/_gate_helpers.py` (new)
#     — shared helper module extracted per locked plan D-A3.7. Carries
#     path canonicalisation (_workspace_relative), mode-bit query
#     (workspace_mode_or_normal_use), sentinel reader wrapper
#     (read_active_scope_sentinel_or_none), tracker open
#     (open_tracker), carve-out detection (is_carve_out_path,
#     _CARVE_OUT_PREFIXES, _CARVE_OUT_FILES), audit-log appender
#     (append_audit_line). Stdlib only; lazy imports for
#     workspace-mode + sentinel reader so a system-Python invocation
#     still falls through to allow.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/tdd_guard.py` (new) —
#     PreToolUse hook script. Stdlib + _gate_helpers + A1 substrate
#     reads only. Fires on Edit|Write|MultiEdit AFTER A2's gate.
#     Decision chain: NORMAL USE → no-op; non-source-tool → no-op;
#     foreign path → allow; carve-out → allow; test-tree path →
#     allow (chicken-and-egg avoidance); missing sentinel → allow
#     (A2 already denied; defensive fall-through); for each binding
#     whose manifest row's created_at is strictly after the
#     sentinel's created_at (NEW AC in this diff) and whose glob
#     admits the path: filename + function-name pinning required —
#     `framework/<comp>/tests/test_AC_<Y-normalised>_*.py` must
#     exist AND contain a function whose name starts with
#     `test_AC_<Y-normalised>_`. Missing test file → deny with
#     missing-test-file failure-class. File present, function
#     absent → deny with missing-test-function failure-class. NDJSON
#     audit log appended on every fire.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/objective_binding_gate.py`
#     — REFACTORED in-place to consume `_gate_helpers.py`. Carve-out
#     prefix/file lists, `_is_carve_out_path`, `_workspace_relative`,
#     `_open_tracker`, `_audit_log_path`, `_append_audit_line` move
#     into the shared helper. A2's behaviour is preserved byte-for-
#     byte; A2's existing AC.OBG.1..AC.OBG.7 + AC.OBG.S +
#     AC.OBG.settings_merge tests pass byte-for-byte against the
#     post-extraction module. Module-level shim re-exports the
#     extracted symbols so existing test imports keep working without
#     a test-file rename.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_settings.py`
#     — `merge_pre_tool_use` extended to multi-contributor:
#     `_POS_V2_PRE_TOOL_USE_COMMAND_MARKERS` adds
#     `tdd_guard.py`. The `_is_pos_v2_owned_pre_tool_use` predicate
#     accepts a stanza whose every inner-hook command matches one of
#     the recognised pos-v2 markers — single-contributor (A2 only)
#     and multi-contributor (A2 + A3) shapes are both pos-v2-owned
#     and may be replaced without a backup. The merge function's
#     signature now accepts `new_entries` (list) OR `new_entry`
#     (single, kept for backwards compat); `new_entries` overrides
#     when both are present. The OUTER PreToolUse list is composed
#     as the supplied list of stanzas in caller-supplied order.
#     Single-contributor callers (A2's previous shape) continue to
#     pass `new_entry=` and produce byte-identical settings.json
#     output to pre-A3 — A2's existing AC.OBG.settings_merge tests
#     pass byte-for-byte.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/first_run_helper.py`
#     — extends `_objective_binding_gate_stanza` neighbours with a
#     new `_tdd_guard_stanza` builder. The existing
#     `_maybe_merge_pre_tool_use` call site now composes BOTH gates
#     into the multi-contributor list (A2 first, A3 second) per
#     locked plan D-A3.8. Fail-soft.
#   - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/test_AC_TDG_1_*.py` ..
#     `test_AC_TDG_S_*.py` plus `test_AC_TDG_8_helper_extraction*.py`
#     and `test_AC_TDG_settings_merge.py` — the AC suite covering
#     the seven behaviours plus seal-diff invariant plus helper-
#     extraction equivalence (D-A3.7 approved → AC.TDG.8 added).
#     Per ODD §8.2.14 byte-content verification, the audit-log test
#     reads the on-disk NDJSON file and asserts schema.
#
# AC surface (AC.TDG.1 – AC.TDG.S, AC.TDG.8) — outcome-shaped per
# the locked plan §4. Behaviour count = 8 + invariant + helper-
# extraction-regression = 9; ACs declared = 9. Forward + reverse
# match.
#
# Helper-library extraction is in scope per locked plan hard
# constraint 18 (D-A3.7 approved). The refactor moves shared logic
# out of `objective_binding_gate.py` into `_gate_helpers.py`; A2's
# behaviour is preserved (A2's existing AC.OBG.x suite is the
# regression contract; AC.TDG.8 is the explicit equivalence AC).
# AC.OBG.S frozen-both-endpoints invariant is untouched — its
# endpoints close before A3 begins (A2 sealed at #70 with both
# BASELINE and SEAL_COMMIT pinned; AC.OBG.S window does not
# extend).
#
# Hook-chain ordering: A2 first, A3 second per D-A3.8. A3 runs the
# FULL decision chain (defensive duplication of mode + carve-out +
# sentinel-presence checks) so the gate is self-contained against
# hook-chain reordering, A2 removal, and asymmetric carve-out lists.
# A2's deny short-circuits A3 (Claude Code stops chain on first
# deny); when A3 runs, A2 has already admitted the path.
#
# Mode bit short-circuits A3 to no-op in NORMAL USE (D-A3.6 / D4
# programme lock — ODD-discipline gate is DEV-MODE-only).
#
# AC normalisation rule (D-A3.9 method per ODD §7.4): drop leading
# `AC.` if present; replace `.` with `_`; uppercase. So `AC.TDG.1`
# normalises to `TDG_1`; the test-file glob is `test_AC_TDG_1_*.py`
# and the function-name prefix is `test_AC_TDG_1_`. Verified at
# build start by reading existing test names across all framework
# components (objective-tracker, hands-off-lifecycle, orchestrator,
# workspace-bootstrap, primary-persona, memory-system) — every
# `test_AC_*.py` file follows `test_AC_<dot-replaced-with-
# underscore>_*.py` convention. Pre-`AC` legacy names (e.g.
# `test_AC38_*` for orchestrator) are not in scope — those tests
# were authored before the dotted-AC-id convention crystallised.
#
# Audit log shape (D-A3.10 method per ODD §7.4): NDJSON at
# `<workspace>/workspace/.pos/tdd-guard.log` mirroring A2's
# objective-binding-gate.log pattern. Atomic append via POSIX
# O_APPEND for writes < PIPE_BUF.
#
# Self-bootstrap order followed (locked plan hard constraint 16):
# (a) tracker manifest rows registered for AC.TDG.1..AC.TDG.S +
# AC.TDG.8 BEFORE first source edit (the build agent's authoring
# discipline); (b) A3's tests authored BEFORE A3's source files
# (test files admitted by A3's own test-tree carve-out, AC.TDG.3);
# (c) A3's source files authored last. This bootstrap order
# satisfies BOTH A2 (rows registered → A2 admits) AND A3 (tests
# authored before source for new ACs → A3 admits).
#
# ODD §2.5 reverse-direction audit clean: every code path,
# branch, dependency, and test in the diff traces back to a
# named AC. No silent exception branches; no defensive `if`
# for cases the ACs do not name; no method-in-AC drift.
#
# Out of scope (locked plan-doc §7, named explicitly):
#
#   - A4 Bash/Agent-context guards.
#   - Direction B (test-without-implementation refusal).
#   - Test quality validation (body correctness, assertion strength).
#   - Dispatcher-side test-author-on-dispatch wrapper.
#   - Audit-log rotation.
#   - Cross-amendment manifest queries.
#   - Test-file deletion detection.
#   - Persona-side surfacing of A3 deny diagnostics.
#   - Composition with FIDRAFT-130 corpus-inlining.
#   - Composition with FIDRAFT-136 main-session-write-prevention.
#   - Audit-log consumers (FIDRAFT-143 dispatch-staleness, etc.).
#   - Helper-library expansion beyond what A3 needs.
#   - Settings.json migration on existing workspaces.
